# Part of the "venus3d" module -- see venus3dService.js's installVtestSocketProp() for the
# full story. minigbm's own patched NVIDIA backend (external/minigbm/nvidia_venus.c in this
# project's AOSP tree, nvidia_venus_connect()) does not read the VTEST_SOCKET_NAME environment
# variable Mesa's Vulkan ICD uses (vn_renderer_create_vtest(), set via surfaceflinger.rc's own
# setenv) -- it reads this system property instead, via __system_property_get(), falling back to
# a hardcoded /dev/venus/venus.sock (not this module's actual socket path) if unset. Without this,
# any gralloc.cros.so consumer -- most importantly the legacy HIDL 2.0 Allocator service
# SurfaceFlinger's own GraphicBufferAllocator depends on for real display buffers -- fails with
# ENODEV ("no vtest connection") and crash-loops.
on early-init
    setprop mesa.vtest.socket.name /vendor/venus.sock
